# Architecture guardrails

**Owners:** docs/engineering/architecture/application-layering.md, docs/ops/code-quality-and-refactor.md

- Thin HTTP/UI shells; domain owns persistence and side effects.
- One coordinator per write concern; no parallel v2 write path without a removal plan.
- First-pass splits: feature folder + index that re-exports only the external surface.
- Delete or inline unused scaffolding before wrapping; named owner destination for "for later".
- Do not raise architecture ratchet ceilings to unblock CI; extract and tighten.
